     "warmer" — it is shorter sentences, no idioms, and no cleverness. -->

## Tone attributes

Three to five named attributes, each with a *because*. More than five and nobody remembers them; a
list without reasons gets argued about every time copy is reviewed.

For each attribute, the useful part is the tension it resolves — what it is chosen **over**.
"Warm, not chummy" is actionable. "Warm" alone is not.

<!-- DECIDE: your attributes, each as "X, not Y" with one line of why. -->

Also state where tone **shifts**: error states, confirmations, and anything destructive usually need
a different register from marketing surfaces. A single flat voice across all of them reads as
tone-deaf at exactly the moments that matter.

